(Metadata)#h3{margin-left:.6em}

  We shouldn't forget to note that these last three tags (script, style and link) were new in the sense that they don't isolate content#b of their own that we'd like to display. These are called metadata#b tags, and they modify the display of other elements in the document - which means they are ideally processed before them. While being careful to place them first could be sufficient, or it may even be fine to adjust the document in retrospect, some metadata tags contain semantic information about the entire document that may be critical for its display, or be of interest before the content, such as <meta>#b tags for description#b, encoding#b and intended screen dimensions#b. For this reason, the main <html>#b tag is divided by respective <head>#b and <body>#b tags, following a namespace declaration as part of the GML standard: 

